  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Nastya and Kostya watch from the bar. They discuss Max and Victoria. We'll hear it in Russian first; don't worry about catching every word. Let's listen closely to their conversation in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Максим молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он помог Вике.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он спас вечер.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, она наговорила гадости.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ему всякие гадости.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И ей очень стыдно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "И как же она это исправит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Что она будет делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А, водка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она нальёт ему водки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Это хороший план.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она знает, что делать.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's go through it line by line. Kostya nods toward Max.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Максим молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maxim did great.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'Maxim' straight to 'well done'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он помог Вике.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He helped Vika.' The first content word means 'he', and 'Vika' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он спас вечер.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He saved the evening.' A compact expression built around 'he' and 'evening'. And Nastya jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, она наговорила гадости.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yeah, she said awful things.' Nastya puts 'it' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'said'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ему всякие гадости.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'All sorts of awful things to him.' The key word here means 'him', which Nastya combines with 'any'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И ей очень стыдно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And she feels terrible.' Nastya starts with 'to her' and pairs it with 'very much' to make the point clear. Kostya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "И как же она это исправит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So how's she going to make it right?' Kostya puts 'how' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'it'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Что она будет делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What will she do?' In Russian, 'what' leads into 'do' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А, водка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Ah, vodka.' The first content word means 'vodka', and 'vodka' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она нальёт ему водки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She will pour him vodka.' Notice the word order: 'it' comes first, and 'vodka' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Это хороший план.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That's a good plan.' Listen for the word meaning 'this' right alongside 'good' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она знает, что делать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She knows what to do.' The question word for 'what' comes right at the start, followed directly by 'do'. Now let's hear the whole scene once more, start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
